                <pb facs="0724" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119P43/844: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Commission to Negotiate
                        Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-03T14:00:00-05:00">December 3, 1919—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3948. Confidential for Polk. Your No. 5531 of December 2, 6 p.m. The President
                    has stated that his decision which was communicated to you in my telegram No.
                    3941 of December 2, 4 p.m. was to be regarded as final.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
